001: spec:
002:   grid: 8-16 rows x 8-16 cols, square [observed]
003:   background: 7 (orange) [observed]; must be most frequent color
004:   corner_objects:
005:     count: 3-4, each anchored at a distinct grid corner (bbox touches both borders forming that corner)
006:     bbox: 1-4 rows x 1-4 cols; must include the corner pixel itself
007:     pixels: 2-12; density 0.62-1.0 (most are fully filled rectangles)
008:     color: monochromatic, non-background; colors may repeat across corners
009:     constraint: for adjacent occupied corners on same edge, sum of their extent along that edge < grid dimension (ensures stamps don't overlap)
010:   distractors:
011:     count: 4-14 (scales with grid size); small monochromatic 4-connected blobs
012:     bbox: 1-5 rows x 1-4 cols; pixels 1-5
013:     placement: scattered in grid interior or touching at most one border (never two adjacent borders forming a corner)
014:     colors: may share colors with corner objects or each other
015:   rule: |
016:     Copy each corner-anchored object clockwise to the next corner (TL->TR, TR->BR, BR->BL, BL->TL).
017:     Orientation is preserved; the copy's bbox is aligned to the destination corner.
018:     Copies overwrite whatever is underneath (including existing corner objects).
019:     Source objects remain in place.
020: 
021: generation_strategy:
022:   approach: output-first
023:   steps:
024:     1. Choose grid size N x N (8-16).
025:     2. Pick 3-4 corners to occupy. For each, generate a small monochromatic shape (1-4 x 1-4 bbox, density >= 0.6, must include corner pixel) with a non-bg color.
026:     3. Verify non-overlap constraint - for each pair of adjacent occupied corners sharing an edge, ensure their bbox extents along that edge sum to less than grid dimension.
027:     4. Build output by stamping each corner object at the next-clockwise corner on top of the base grid.
028:     5. Derive input by removing the clockwise stamps from the output (restore background or the original corner object pixels underneath).
029:     6. Place 4-14 distractor blobs (1-5 pixels each) in positions that do not touch two adjacent borders. Distractors appear identically in input and output.
===== /home/lixinyu/snap/new/spce_dis/arc2_eval/4c416de3_spec.yaml =====
001: spec:
002:   grid:
003:     size: 18-24 rows x 18-24 cols
004:     bg: any color in 1-9 (single solid bg fill)
005:   frames:
006:     count: 2-3 hollow rectangles of 0
007:     shape: axis-aligned rectangles, inner side 3-7 (so outer dims 5-9 per side); mostly square [observed]
008:     completeness: most fully drawn; 0-1 partial (L-shape or edge-truncated rect where one/two sides are shorter than the full bbox)
009:     non_overlap: frames do not overlap; leave >=1 bg cell gap between frames and from grid border (except partial frames at grid edge)
010:   pattern (canonical TL-oriented glyph, shared across the whole grid):
011:     cells: 4-6 offsets, all within |dr|,|dc| <= 3
012:     structure: includes 2+ outward cells (dr<0 or dc<0, forming the outer "tail") AND 1+ inward-diagonal cells (k,k) with k>=1
013:     symmetry: diagonally symmetric about dr==dc axis (every (dr,dc) has mirror (dc,dr))
014:   corners:
015:     every detectable frame-corner is either a source or a target (no inert corners)
016:     source: has the pattern fully pre-drawn, rotated to its kind, in one painted color (not bg, not 0). A frame may contain 1 or more source corners; all sources (across all frames) share the same canonical pattern.
017:     target: has exactly one colored marker pixel at canonical offset (k_max, k_max) rotated to its kind, where k_max is the pattern's largest inward-diagonal k. Marker color is that corner's output color; it may repeat across corners/frames.
018:   transform (input -> output):
019:     for every target corner, paint the canonical pattern (rotated to that corner's TL/TR/BL/BR orientation) using that corner's marker color, onto bg/0 cells (marker pixel is preserved/overwritten with same color)
020: 
021: generation_strategy: |
022:   Output-first construction (build finished output, then derive input by erasing non-source patterns).
023:   1. Pick grid H,W in 18-24; pick bg in 1-9.
024:   2. Design the canonical pattern:
025:      - pick k_max in 1-2; include at least one outward pair like {(-1,0),(0,-1)} or {(-1,-1),(-1,0),(0,-1)}; optionally include (0,0); include diagonal cells {(k,k) for k=1..k_max}; for any non-diagonal cell (dr,dc) also add mirror (dc,dr). Keep |dr|,|dc|<=3 and 4-6 cells total.
026:   3. Place 2-3 non-overlapping hollow 0-frames: random square sizes 5-8 per side, >=1 cell gap from each other and borders. Optionally truncate one frame into an L-shape or let it touch a grid edge.
027:   4. Pick 1-2 source corners (may be in the same frame, e.g. two opposite corners, or in different frames). Assign an output color to every remaining detectable corner (each corner's color is independent; colors may repeat across corners).
028:   5. Render the output: draw 0-frames; at each source corner paint the pattern (rotated to its kind) in that source's color; at every non-source corner paint the pattern (rotated to its kind) in that corner's output color.
029:   6. Derive input from output: for every non-source corner, erase all painted cells of its pattern back to bg/0 except keep only the marker pixel at rotated (k_max,k_max) in that corner's color. Source corners retain their full pattern.
030:   7. Sanity-check: running the solver on the input reproduces the output exactly.
